## RINGKASAN

Primary Ecosystem: Ethereum Layer 2 / Superchain (OP Stack chains)
Supported Chains: OP Mainnet (primary), Ethereum (L1), Base, World Chain, Zora Network, Mode, Fraxtal, Lyra, 30+ OP Stack chains via Superchain Registry
External Dependencies: 25+ verified (Ethereum L1, OP Stack components, Cannon, EIP-4844, Standard Bridge, RPC providers Alchemy/Infura/QuickNode, The Graph, Etherscan, CoinGecko, GitHub, Discord, Security auditors Trail of Bits/OpenZeppelin/Spearbit/Sigma Prime, Investors Paradigm/a16z, Fast bridges Hop/Across/Synapse, Oracles Chainlink/Pyth, Interop LayerZero/Wormhole, Kubernetes/Prometheus/Grafana/Loki, Cloud providers)
Major Integrations: 12+ verified (Base, World Chain, Zora Network, Mode, Fraxtal, Lyra, Superchain Registry, Granite Interop planned, Optimism Gateway, Airdrops #3-4 cross-Superchain, RetroPGF cross-ecosystem)
Infrastructure Providers: 15+ verified (RPC: Alchemy, Infura, QuickNode, Chainstack, Rivet; Explorers: Etherscan, Blockscout; Indexing: The Graph, Alchemy Subgraphs, Envio; CI/CD: GitHub Actions; Container: Docker Hub/GHCR; Cloud: AWS/GCP/Azure; Observability: Prometheus/Grafana/Alertmanager/Loki)
Developer Programs: 4 grant programs (Optimism Foundation Grants, RetroPGF, OP Labs Ecosystem Grants, Superchain Builder Grants), 2+ hackathon series (ETHGlobal, OP Stack Hackathons), comprehensive SDK/tooling (TypeScript SDK, viem/ethers, Hardhat, Foundry, OP Stack CLI, local devnet)
Applications: 30+ verified across DeFi (Velodrome, Aerodrome, Synthetix, Kwenta, Lyra, Polynomial, Sonne, Granary, Beefy, Yearn, Uniswap, Curve, Balancer, Aave), Bridges (Hop, Across, Synapse, LayerZero, Wormhole), Oracles (Chainlink, Pyth), Indexing (The Graph, Envio), NFTs (Zora, OpenSea, SuperRare, Quix), Explorers (Etherscan, Blockscout), Tools (Gateway, CoinGecko)

## Open Threads

- Complete list of 30+ OP Stack chains in Superchain Registry — only 7 mainnet chains identified (Base, World Chain, Zora Network, Mode, Fraxtal, Lyra, OP Mainnet); 23+ chains (testnet/devnet/planned) not fully documented with status
- Granite upgrade exact mainnet activation timeline — testnet testing ongoing, no confirmed mainnet date
- Permissionless fault proof (Cannon/op-challenger) mainnet deployment date — Stage 2 decentralization target not officially announced
- Shared sequencing design specifications — Granite interop specs published but shared sequencing mechanics details limited
- Forced inclusion / escape hatch mechanism for sequencer censorship — mentioned in roadmap but no published spec
- OP Labs enterprise revenue (RPC services, consulting) — not confirmed publicly
- Exact RPC provider market share distribution — no public metrics on traffic split between Alchemy, Infura, QuickNode, others
- Security Council multi-sig signer identities and threshold — not fully public
- Citizens' House badge holder count, selection criteria, and OP holder overlap — not published in aggregate
- Delegation participation rate (percentage of OP supply actively delegated) — not in official metrics
- Cross-chain OP token representations (bridged OP on Ethereum L1, Base, other chains) — canonical only on OP Mainnet L2; bridged versions exist but not officially tracked
- RetroPGF Round 4 exact OP amount — blog announces completion but no nominal disclosure
- Airdrop #5+ criteria and timeline — Foundation signals future airdrops but no published schedule
- OP staking design for shared sequencing — ethresear.ch discussions exist but no formal spec or governance proposal
- State growth mitigation research status — no formal proposal for Optimism-specific state expiry
- Legal classification of OP token (utility vs security) — Foundation maintains utility stance but no regulatory no-action letter
- Exact revenue split post-Canyon (base fee burn vs priority fee to sequencer vs protocol) — requires on-chain analysis
- Impact of EIP-4844 blobs on sequencer revenue model post-Fjord — no official analysis published